# `dist/` is committed on purpose: the plugin ships as a marketplace git checkout
# into ~/.claude/plugins/cache/, and Claude Code never runs a build on install or
# autoUpdate. The lifecycle hooks invoke ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/dist/cli.js, so the
# built CLI must travel inside the published commit or the hooks silently no-op.
# red-memory-dist-check.yml enforces that the committed dist matches src/.
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
